# Are there more bacteria in your body than human cells?
subtitle: "Do bacteria outnumber your own cells ten to one? Guess, then watch the famous ratio shrink and learn why one trip to the toilet can tip it."

## Are there more bacteria in your body than human cells?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Human cells
      - Bacteria
    values:
      - [10, 100]
      - [30, 38]
      - [30, 27]
    stage: 0
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 110
    y_label: Trillions
    box:
      x: 90
      'y': 200
      w: 560
      h: 440
sources:
    - id: sender
      title: Revised estimates for the number of human and bacteria cells in the body
      authors: R. Sender, S. Fuchs, R. Milo
      year: 2016
      doi: 10.1371/journal.pbio.1002533
      finding: about 3.8e13 bacteria and 3.0e13 human cells (ratio about 1.3:1); red blood cells are about 84 % of human cells; bacteria weigh about 0.2 kg; each defecation may flip the ratio
    - id: luckey
      title: Introduction to intestinal microecology
      authors: T. D. Luckey
      year: 1972
      finding: the rough estimate of 10^14 bacteria behind the 10:1 claim

    text old "the old 10 : 1" #8f887c x 800 y 600 font_size 40 hidden true
    text new "2016: 1 : 1" #b5482e cites ["sender"] x 800 y 520 font_size 40 hidden true
    text loo "one toilet trip" #2f6b8f x 800 y 300 font_size 36 hidden true
    mark old_x around old kind strike hidden true
    path rbc dashed thick #b5482e points [[-0.45,25],[0.45,25]] data true hidden true
    text rbc_l "red cells" #b5482e at.data [0,21.5] font_size 28 hidden true
    icon toilet size 110 set twemoji x 800 y 400 icon_look picture of toilet hidden true

    card title "More bacteria than human cells?"

Are there more bacteria living in your body than human cells?
    draw axes

    quiz "How do the bacteria in your body compare with your own cells?"
        right: About one each.
        wrong: The famous answer is out of date.
        * Ten bacteria per cell
        + About one each
        * Far fewer bacteria

For decades, textbooks said bacteria outnumber us ten to one.
    draw bar_1 bar_2 old

But that began as a rough guess in 1972, and was copied for forty years.
    highlight bar_2

In 2016, scientists at the Weizmann Institute counted again, and the gap shrank to nearly even.
    animate stage 1 ylim.1 45 duration 2.5

Ron Sender, Shai Fuchs and Ron Milo found about thirty-eight trillion bacteria
    draw new old_x

to thirty trillion human cells.
    highlight bar_1

Most of your own cells turn out to be red blood cells: tiny, and very many.
    draw rbc rbc_l

And the bacteria, mostly in the colon, weigh only about two hundred grams in all.
    highlight bar_2

In fact the two are so close that, as the auth (@draw loo toilet@)ors noted, one trip to the toilet can tip the balance back toward you.

Flush, and for a little while, you are mostly you again.
    animate stage 2 duration 2
---
